@startuml fig3_flows
' Diagram 3 of the VDI 3682 pattern: the flow, and the two forms it takes.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: how a flow connects a state with an operator, and the two
' special forms Part 1 gives it.
'
' The flow is a class rather than an edge. Part 1 draws it as an arrow, and
' reifying it is what lets a model identify one, annotate it, and mark it as
' parallel or alternative. That is why it needs a diagram of its own: four
' source and target relations run between the same three classes, and drawing
' them alongside the states of diagram 2 stacks their labels.
'
' A flow runs from a state to an operator or from an operator to a state, never
' from an operator to an operator. The four relations below are what states
' that, and the general hasSource and hasTarget above them are left out: they
' carry no information a drawing can show.
'
' State and ProcessOperator each appear in two boxes, once per role. Drawing
' them once would put four edges between two boxes and stack their labels, and
' the roles are what the diagram is about.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - the kinds of state: diagram 2
'  - resources and their assignment: diagram 4

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

' The two directions a flow can run are drawn as two rows rather than as four
' edges between two boxes. State and ProcessOperator each appear twice, once as
' a source and once as a target, which is what a flow connects: the classes are
' the same, the roles are not.
class "State" as SourceState
class "ProcessOperator" as TargetOperator
class "ProcessOperator" as SourceOperator
class "State" as TargetState

class Flow
class ParallelFlow
class AlternativeFlow

Flow <|-- ParallelFlow
Flow <|-- AlternativeFlow

Flow --> "1" SourceState    : hasStateSource
Flow --> "1" TargetOperator : hasOperatorTarget
Flow --> "1" SourceOperator : hasOperatorSource
Flow --> "1" TargetState    : hasStateTarget

' Layout only: the incoming pair on one row, the outgoing pair on the next.
SourceState    -[hidden]right- TargetOperator
SourceOperator -[hidden]right- TargetState
ParallelFlow   -[hidden]right- AlternativeFlow

@enduml
